<ResourceDictionary xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation" xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">

    <!--
        ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        MediCore ViewModel → View DataTemplate Registry
        
        Maps every ViewModel type to its View so any ContentControl
        bound to a ViewModel instance (the Shell's content area via
        IContentService, and ModalService's modal host) renders the
        right XAML automatically — no manual DataTemplateSelector,
        no switch statement in code-behind.
        
        IMPORTANT: This dictionary must be merged into Application
        resources (see App.xaml), NOT into a single View's resources.
        Implicit DataTemplates (keyed by DataType, no x:Key) are only
        picked up by a ContentPresenter if they're visible somewhere
        in the resource lookup chain above it — merging at App level
        guarantees both ShellView's content area AND ModalService's
        modal host (a separate ContentControl) can resolve them.
        Previously this lived in ShellView.Resources, which happened
        to work only because both content areas were nested inside
        Shell — fragile if that ever changes.
        ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
    -->

